✅ Strong Interview Answer

Even if a user has the AdministratorAccess policy, they may still be unable to delete an S3 bucket if there is an explicit deny applied somewhere in the permission evaluation chain.

The explicit deny could come from:

A Service Control Policy (SCP) in AWS Organizations

A permission boundary

A resource-based policy like an S3 bucket policy

A session policy

Since explicit deny overrides allow, AWS will block the action even if AdministratorAccess is attached.

